The words of Allah, the Exalted: ﴿The likeness of those who disbelieve in their Lord is that their deeds are like ashes on which the wind blows violently on a stormy day﴾, and so on.

Allah, the Exalted, struck a parable in this noble verse for the deeds of the disbelievers, using ashes that the winds blow violently on a stormy day, meaning a day of intense wind. Just as that fierce, stormy wind scatters the ashes and leaves no trace of them, so too the deeds of the disbelievers, such as maintaining ties of kinship, hospitality toward guests, relieving the distress of the afflicted, and kindness to one's parents, and the like, are nullified and destroyed by disbelief, just as that wind scatters those ashes. He struck other parables in other verses for the deeds of the disbelievers with this same meaning, such as:

• His saying: ﴿And those who disbelieve, their deeds are like a mirage in a level plain, which the thirsty one thinks is water, until, when he comes to it, he finds it to be nothing﴾ [al-Nur: 39];

• His saying: ﴿The likeness of what they spend in this worldly life is like a wind containing frost that strikes the tilth of a people who have wronged themselves (p-246) and destroys it﴾ [Ali 'Imran: 117], and the rest of the verse;

• His saying: ﴿O you who believe, do not nullify your charities with reminders and injury, like one who spends his wealth to be seen by people and does not believe in Allah and the Last Day. His likeness is like a smooth rock with a little dust on it; a heavy rain strikes it and leaves it bare. They have no power over anything of what they have earned. And Allah does not guide the disbelieving people﴾ [al-Baqarah: 264];

• His saying: ﴿And We will turn to what they did of deeds and make them scattered dust﴾ [al-Furqan: 23],

and other verses besides these.

In another place He explained that the wisdom in His striking parables is that people may reflect upon them, so that they understand a matter at a glance. This is His saying: ﴿And these are the parables We strike for the people, that perhaps they will reflect﴾ [al-Hashr: 21]. Similar to it is His saying: ﴿And Allah strikes parables for the people, that perhaps they will remember﴾ [Ibrahim: 25]. In another place He explained that parables are not understood except by people of knowledge, as in His saying, exalted is He: ﴿And these are the parables We strike for the people, and none understands them except the knowledgeable﴾ [al-'Ankabut: 43]. In another place He explained that the parable He strikes becomes, by Allah's making, a cause of guidance for a people who understand it, and a cause of misguidance for a people who do not grasp its wisdom. This is His saying: ﴿As for those who believed, they know that it is the truth from their Lord; but as for those who disbelieved, they say, "What did Allah intend by this as an example?" He misleads thereby many and guides thereby many. And He misleads thereby none except the defiantly disobedient﴾ [al-Baqarah: 26]. In another place He explained that He, exalted is He, is not shy to strike a parable of any kind, even if the parable struck is a gnat or something greater. It was said: "or something smaller than it," because it surpasses it in smallness; and it was said: "or something greater than it," meaning something larger than it. This is His saying: ﴿Indeed, Allah is not shy to strike a parable, be it a gnat or what is above it﴾ [al-Baqarah: 26]. For this reason He struck the parable of the spider in His saying: ﴿The likeness of those who take other than Allah as allies is like the spider that makes for itself a house; and indeed, the frailest of houses is the spider's house, if only they knew﴾ [al-'Ankabut: 41]. He struck the parable of the donkey in His saying: ﴿Like the example of a donkey carrying volumes﴾ and the rest of the verse [al-Jumu'ah: 5]. He struck the parable of the dog in His saying: ﴿And had We willed, We would have elevated him thereby, but he adhered to the earth and followed his desire. So his example is like that of the dog: if you chase him, he pants, or if you leave him, he pants﴾ [al-A'raf: 176], and other than that. And knowledge is with Allah, the Exalted.
